# Shell scripts that run inside the Linux containers must not be checked out
# with CRLF. `core.autocrlf=true` is normal on a Windows checkout, and a file
# whose first line is `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a script the kernel can exec: the
# image builds, then dies on start with "exec: ... no such file or directory".
docker/*.sh text eol=lf
# Same reason for the refresh script a developer runs from a Windows checkout:
# `set -eu\r` is not `set -eu`, so a CRLF checkout makes it fail before Docker.
scripts/refresh_lock.sh text eol=lf
